[
  {
    "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The composition features two shallow white matte ceramic bowls placed on a rustic, weathered oak wooden surface, shot from a 3/4 overhead angle to showcase the volume of the ingredients. The primary bowl is sharp in the immediate foreground, with the second bowl softly blurred behind it. Each bowl is composed with a base of crisp, chopped green romaine lettuce, topped with distinct mounds of nutty-brown rice, whole pinto beans, and crumbles of lean ground beef that show a rich, dark spice-rubbed texture with a slight glistening sheen from the broth reduction. Fresh, vibrant pico de gallo with bright red tomato chunks and white onion bits is tucked to one side, alongside cubes of pale green, creamy avocado. Chopped fresh cilantro is scattered naturally over the top. A wooden spoon lies casually on the oak surface next to the foreground bowl. A small, crumpled linen napkin sits partially beneath one side of the bowls. Lighting is soft and natural, coming from a window on the left, casting gentle, diffused shadows. The scene displays slight, authentic imperfections: a small streak of sauce on the rim, a few stray cilantro leaves and a single stray bean on the wood surface, and an asymmetric distribution of toppings. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene should look like someone just finished cooking and plating — lived-in, warm, authentic. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces, no perfect symmetry. Warm, golden-hour color temperature — cozy and inviting. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. Indistinguishable from a professional cookbook photograph."
  }
]
